# 🐞 bug report

### Description

This issue follows https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/35615#

I am trying to update our [project](https://github.com/quentin-ol/ngx-openlayers) in angular 9.
Everything is fine, except that I get this warning when I consume the library.

I try to use `ngcc.config.js` to avoid the warning message but it doesn't work.
```
// architecture
projects/
    ngx-openlayers/  <----- lib with ol in peerDependencies
      ng-package.json
/src                 <----- demo project
ngcc.config.js       <----- i put ngcc.config.js here
```
```js
// ngcc.config.js
module.exports = {
  packages: {
    'ngx-openlayers': {
      ignorableDeepImportMatchers: [
        /ol\//,
      ]
    },
  },
};
```
I also don't really understand how this configuration will work once the library is deployed.

## 🔬 Minimal Reproduction
https://github.com/kekel87/ngx-openlayers/tree/chore-update-to-angular-9
```
ng build ngx-openlayers --prod
ng serve
```

## 🔥 Exception or Error
<pre><code>WARNING in Entry point 'ngx-openlayers' contains deep imports into
  '[pwd]/ngx-openlayers/node_modules/ol/View',
  '[pwd]/ngx-openlayers/node_modules/ol/Map',
  '[pwd]/ngx-openlayers/node_modules/ol/layer',
</code></pre>

